              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ymlljcd"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Fantastic, simple recipe. I substituted Splenda for the sugar &amp; omitted the cocoa. Upped the Vanilla &amp; Cinnamon to 1t. Added 4 slices of bread &amp; 4 snack-size boxes of raisins (which were boiled in water to soften). Used a 9x11 Pyrex dish (without the water); baked for 30-35 minutes.",
            "datePublished": "2023-04-16T16:25:45.794Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jane"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I doubled the recipe , and used a 9 x 13 pyrex dish. I used left over large Mary B’s biscuits. About 9-11 biscuits crumbled to fill the pan . \nI did add extra cinnamon as we like a bit extra . \nI replaced the oil with real butter.\nDidn’t have milk so I used cream. I had medium eggs so used 5 . \nI sprinkled the top with sugar and cinnamon. \nI did cook it longer - till center didn’t jighle and it was golden brown. \nI really wanted to add toasted pecans but some of our family are anti nuts in food. Strange. \nEveryone liked it a lot. \nI’ll make it again \nJane",
            "datePublished": "2021-07-28T23:48:49.133Z"
          },
